DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The bbccmmssttbbppiinnccttrrll driver uses pin control data from the device tree to
     select one of multiple possible roles available for pins on Broadcom Set-
     top Box SoCs.  This includes the Broadcom BCM2712 SoC that is used in the
     Raspberry Pi 5.  It does not provide direct device driver entry points
     but makes its functions available to other drivers.

